# port-patches.sh: glm/sampling-r7 @ 3c8b05d8bbb7 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 1ea862b590e4..95526fcaa650); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: an offline test that every Triton lookup at TP=2, up to a 1,048,576-token window, is in the captured kernel set; TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE=1 with KV sharding warns instead of refusing

The recipe pins CONTEXT=131072 at TP=2, and nothing showed a longer window
finds every kernel variant it launches (the lookup has no context key).

- cuda_aot_coverage_test.zig (new) runs the engine's own launch code
  (Engine.chunk, dsaLayer, Forward.compute) against a driver that only hands
  out addresses, and looks each Triton launch up in the captured set
  (zig/tests/cuda/glm_p1/aot/aot.json) as aot.Set.find would: prompt chunks of
  every row count a prompt can have (a multiple of 64 up to 2,048, or the last
  1..63 rows: the pass cuts at the 64-token grid), the row split off and on,
  both ranks; the DSA layer at every position under the dense limit and every
  selection class past it; decode windows of 1..64 rows over each pool's
  decode scratch. 80 configurations: CONTEXT 131072 to 1048576, PARALLEL 8
  and 4, pools of 825,344 to 4,194,304 rows and their KV-shard parts. None
  missing (known_missing is empty). Random prompts' chunks check that the
  representatives stand for every chunk; a mutant set without CP=256 checks
  the sweep reports a gap where it is reached. TF_GLM_AOT_COVERAGE_ALL_ROWS=1
  (a diagnostic) sweeps every row count: then the prompt-block selection of a
  block under 64 rows is missing (_select_split OUT int64 SEG=0 VIS=0 TOKS=0,
  _select_rows BLOCK=4096 VIS=0, _scores R=1), which no chunk the engine makes
  at TP=2 reaches. Recorder.sink hands each launch on instead of saving it.
- TF_GLM_MULTI_LONE=1 with TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1: the Python fork refuses its
  lone-stream decode with sharding; this engine has no lone-stream decode, so
  the setting cannot conflict. cuda_shard.refuse drops KvShardWithLone,
  cuda_shard.warning gives the start-up's words and cuda_native.kvAdmit logs
  them; the settings text keeps lone=, so the ranks still agree on it. The
  shard checks' refuse section and the kvAdmit test failed before the change.

Switches: none new (TF_GLM_AOT_COVERAGE_ALL_ROWS is the test's own). Serving
is unchanged but for the MULTI_LONE start-up line.

Measured on the pair: not run yet (the GPU sweep at 131k/262k/512k/1M is the
next session's).

